#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203865 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d786586f-cacb-5781-86ff-cc8acf311dcf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Total Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "1b970d71-b996-5a49-b024-052c32073518" :question/math-academy-id "e-17864" :question/problem "Consider the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}: \\mathbb{R}^{4} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^2$ defined by\n![](images/2e/2e7f8144a8cb560911b65d4ca657148df69568184b1aca0e89b5551e0d3cdcae.svg)\n\nWhat is $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{f}}{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{x}},$ the total derivative of $\\mathbf{f}$ with respect to $\\mathbf{x}$ at ![](images/ad/adccb3fb0692529551c254d01387a1c1950ff044def046da83d1331fd9271ea1.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}: \\mathbb{R}^{n} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^m$ with respect to a vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ is the $m \\times n$ matrix\n![](images/01/01a79963b1871d82fdd7244b67eb2185cd9bc3e1f066d0def6366552677b32fe.svg)\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $\\mathbf{f}(\\mathbf{x})$ where ![](images/f6/f621db9742637aa006cc2033c77d6d30cf664529fd94cc2db9964effa2c44ed5.svg), we get\n![](images/48/4825869f62821be4a775d58c7e85c03948025be018489cabb460156f74d80a58.svg)\n\nFrom here, we have $f_1(\\mathbf{x}) = x_1 + 2x_2 + 4x_3 + 8x_4$ and $f_2(\\mathbf{x}) = x_1 + 3x_2 + 9x_3 +27x_4.$ So, the total derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{3}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{4}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{3}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{4}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 27\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the total derivative is a constant matrix, evaluating it at ![](images/50/5001c288fe848bed80ed10055323aad27c90d0acab2088baf9fc48ebe17b3f4a.svg) gives the same matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203867 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15fada7f-4a9a-5e72-9699-694e302beef3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a 3-Tensor Derivative"}] :question/id #uuid "981a1177-016a-55ca-9ea7-a92220087d8b" :question/math-academy-id "e-17947" :question/problem "Consider a function $\\mathbf{f}: \\mathbb R^{2\\times 3} \\to \\mathbb R^2$ defined by\n![](images/75/7583605f8c8c3cd07389b8f31c6bfc4eaaf3a6488f226a05d5e0972e5272c2c8.svg)\nGiven that $a_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $\\mathbf{A}$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, find the value of $\\dfrac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial a_{12}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the function $\\mathbf{f}$ as\n![](images/ed/ed6fb0575a19c9afb201170a089841d0271e20e219c54c956e03f5d3e8c87f41.svg)\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial a_{12}} = \\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial a_{12}} (-a_{11} + 3a_{12} + 7a_{13} ) = 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203872 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "feb08dad-d927-55f9-8fef-723795030c8c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Shape of a Derivative"}] :question/id #uuid "56dcfaf0-3600-5f8a-aa49-fa6bcb04ec0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-18007" :question/problem "Consider the function\n![](images/4e/4e1b8017187aa04115950f67cbae8c62e260002d8df6f8fb86339959b8738262.svg)\nwhere the dot denotes matrix multiplication. What is the shape of the total derivative $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{f}}{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{x}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}: \\mathbb{R}^{n} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^m$ with respect to a vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ is the $m \\times n$ matrix\n![](images/84/84a86b7e75b3c09396405d92062543f980f325b4871b591f8d6ad06d1f0fa4cc.svg)\n\nIn our case, the function multiplies a vector by a $2 \\times 4$ matrix. Thus,\n\n- it must act on $4$-dimensional column vectors as input, and\n\n- output a $2$-dimensional column vector.\n\nTherefore, $\\mathbf{f}: \\mathbb{R}^{4} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^2,$ and the total derivative will be a $2 \\times 4$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "feb08dad-d927-55f9-8fef-723795030c8c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Shape of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2b0a77b-04e0-502e-a07b-b33fe49d08d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a scalar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203384} {:answer/id #uuid "00cade8b-82f0-55dd-882c-e41f7d0dbec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a matrix of shape $2\\times 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529575} {:answer/id #uuid "09bcf7d5-0e15-5788-b19a-20530c55b7e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a column vector of shape $2\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529595} {:answer/id #uuid "1dded79a-5b8e-5d4e-92b8-7b2238b34f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a row vector of shape $1\\times 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529641} {:answer/id #uuid "49a1c8e2-507d-5c9d-8224-1f9dc78d98be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a matrix of shape $1\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dded79a-5b8e-5d4e-92b8-7b2238b34f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a row vector of shape $1\\times 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529641} :answer-field/id #uuid "dec38f12-fbfa-5f08-877a-c93999e7e849" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4344fbfa-5be9-5aa7-8380-a9ec89fc169b" :question/math-academy-id "q-268174" :question/problem "Consider the function $f,$ defined as \n\n$$\nf({x}_{1},{x}_{2})={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the shape of the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ and\n\n- outputs a scalar $f({x}_{1},{x}_{2})\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the total derivative will be a row vector of shape $1\\times 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15fada7f-4a9a-5e72-9699-694e302beef3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a 3-Tensor Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4cfa01d-2d08-5b77-b97b-525e3855efcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4cfa01d-2d08-5b77-b97b-525e3855efcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530031} :answer-field/id #uuid "5373309d-7943-5c8a-a6b8-b63761bb74b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56e1e5bd-443d-5461-a5ba-43e3e1a70600" :question/math-academy-id "q-268175" :question/problem "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to {R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=A[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{32}}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11}+2{a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21}+2{a}_{22} \\\\ {a}_{31}+2{a}_{32}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{32}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{32}}({a}_{31}+2{a}_{32})=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d786586f-cacb-5781-86ff-cc8acf311dcf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Total Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "312c6c6d-408c-53ac-981e-a9f933aff470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529688} {:answer/id #uuid "60be3a32-9634-5fc9-af68-57501017072c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529815} {:answer/id #uuid "83803cc0-4654-56d7-9011-c919d719793e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529907} {:answer/id #uuid "8f3d1b6a-19cd-52a6-8624-ea921d4995d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529927} {:answer/id #uuid "946e9d66-f055-53a6-a7ab-d00d690fa74a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f3d1b6a-19cd-52a6-8624-ea921d4995d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529927} :answer-field/id #uuid "2022259d-dab3-5737-825a-bb118d9d5f9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7cc4d26a-41d9-58ba-a0d9-1c9954f5d4a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-268490" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:R\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{2}$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "feb08dad-d927-55f9-8fef-723795030c8c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Shape of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c19ce23-0c31-5068-aed9-32cc8d9c228b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a row vector of shape $1\\times 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529763} {:answer/id #uuid "64968f39-b0c1-5f17-aef4-525928e2645e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a matrix of shape $2\\times 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529829} {:answer/id #uuid "938499fe-a2ba-5bd8-bad4-eea781e881bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a scalar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529940} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce1d5b9-0ed1-5721-9ba6-e9de7b0b4cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a matrix of shape $1\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529969} {:answer/id #uuid "b58c3277-c9bd-5945-ab2e-eab5556bf637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a column vector of shape $2\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b58c3277-c9bd-5945-ab2e-eab5556bf637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a column vector of shape $2\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530033} :answer-field/id #uuid "e55a1031-a1ea-5352-b0ca-33b6092bf496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa63b2c2-42b9-59b8-bd18-614050796969" :question/math-academy-id "q-269269" :question/problem "Consider the function $f,$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the shape of the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the total derivative will be a column vector of shape $2\\times 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "feb08dad-d927-55f9-8fef-723795030c8c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Shape of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c2ea734-3f92-5678-adc3-be49808baf15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a matrix of shape $1\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529600} {:answer/id #uuid "39cb1391-7d4d-5422-beaa-776b609ebd95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a row vector of shape $1\\times 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529714} {:answer/id #uuid "598952e9-2286-5b99-9132-505d762f9575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a scalar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529795} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec12c97-df33-5d9b-8036-15c7caf1bb1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a matrix of shape $3\\times 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529808} {:answer/id #uuid "9da41052-c8ec-5c81-b49d-1fde079f36c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a column vector of shape $3\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9da41052-c8ec-5c81-b49d-1fde079f36c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a column vector of shape $3\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529970} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aac7a31-991e-5902-b2bc-4ac1b08a8cb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530299}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "439b4dea-3b14-5e08-901c-f0507eee5855" :question/math-academy-id "q-269270" :question/problem "Consider the function $f,$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}x-1 \\\\ {x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the shape of the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the total derivative will be a column vector of shape $3\\times 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "feb08dad-d927-55f9-8fef-723795030c8c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Shape of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00a47e43-e30e-5114-9ffb-a4bad244ed6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a matrix of shape $1\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529574} {:answer/id #uuid "2e534c95-f518-53b6-a86e-97ebc796a9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a column vector of shape $3\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529680} {:answer/id #uuid "33c3af05-d4bc-58d9-859f-9ed6f1f1fb54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a scalar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529696} {:answer/id #uuid "4dabe466-88e9-513a-a085-624722b4b785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a row vector of shape $1\\times 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529765} {:answer/id #uuid "fa799a0a-fb3a-50c2-8f68-0582a2824583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a matrix of shape $3\\times 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e534c95-f518-53b6-a86e-97ebc796a9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a column vector of shape $3\\times 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529680} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa645345-9bb6-5b6a-b7b1-5257c890c755" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b8ee097-f47a-59de-984f-4442445eaee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-269311" :question/problem "Consider the function $f,$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere the dot denotes matrix multiplication.\nWhat is the shape of the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the total derivative will be a column vector of shape $3\\times 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "feb08dad-d927-55f9-8fef-723795030c8c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Shape of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c50be14-bf50-50d2-bdeb-b61770748eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a $2\\times 3$ matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529601} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc42ffe-b6bb-55f0-a37a-8ca9e32eca2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a $3\\times 3$ matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529968} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec35115-0e98-54f5-afea-868f2a9083f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a $3$-dimensional row vector" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529973} {:answer/id #uuid "b63c0ad4-aae1-57f3-a48e-f5b928ad9478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a $3\\times 2$ matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530035} {:answer/id #uuid "c8225ab7-6f2d-551b-884d-3c80beac0154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a $3$-dimensional column vector" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cc42ffe-b6bb-55f0-a37a-8ca9e32eca2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a $3\\times 3$ matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529968} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b19f2b-af4c-5f65-9774-3538bb1658e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "173d167b-5e19-5e83-a0ad-faa7a0c92682" :question/math-academy-id "q-269314" :question/problem "Consider the function \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot x,\n$$\n\nwhere the dot denotes matrix multiplication. What is the shape of the total derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function multiplies a vector by a $3\\times 3$ matrix. Thus, \n\n- it must act on $3$-dimensional column vectors as input, and\n\n- output a $3$-dimensional column vector.\n\nTherefore, $f:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3},$ and the total derivative will be a $3\\times 3$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d786586f-cacb-5781-86ff-cc8acf311dcf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Total Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a78d66-ac2f-567f-a995-bb7404dc996f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529585} {:answer/id #uuid "16648459-62e9-5e7f-bf16-aea558ab3b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529624} {:answer/id #uuid "4037b305-cfc6-556c-8651-d534e563bb62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529731} {:answer/id #uuid "5a590e93-aeaf-5485-9454-240d10475316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529797} {:answer/id #uuid "91f3e890-aa4e-5c31-9332-5127c036fff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04a78d66-ac2f-567f-a995-bb7404dc996f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529585} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd22ab92-c545-5049-be79-46a86bc87feb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08a9562a-8441-5804-8199-2cecfe4f52dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-269508" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.$ What is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3},$ and\n\n- outputs a scalar $f(x)\\in R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{3} & 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times 3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the total derivative at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}({x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}0+3(2) & 1+2 & 3(1)+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530430 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d786586f-cacb-5781-86ff-cc8acf311dcf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Total Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36eda5b5-aaa3-50f4-808e-2ebbafdb8d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} & 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529704} {:answer/id #uuid "6d60435b-ec88-5c57-8c2f-2268a47398b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529858} {:answer/id #uuid "de8edb05-08f9-5f50-905f-b752f7df4d7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530136} {:answer/id #uuid "eb57ae0c-4948-524a-bf84-e3e8209d04b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}{x}_{2} & 6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530169} {:answer/id #uuid "f034c121-3677-5359-8feb-3f7fcbaa492b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} & 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d60435b-ec88-5c57-8c2f-2268a47398b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529858} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b271751-4c56-517e-82e7-5413a260d685" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b78008a-d228-5f88-9d88-9b7926941425" :question/math-academy-id "q-269510" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot x,\n$$\n\nwhere the dot denotes matrix multiplication. What is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(x)$ where $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times 2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d786586f-cacb-5781-86ff-cc8acf311dcf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Total Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83b07263-56a1-53d6-9f6b-dd0ec4566cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2x \\\\ 3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529908} {:answer/id #uuid "ae536f43-cb19-5d09-9654-9a4ddf9db7b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ {x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530013} {:answer/id #uuid "b8433fa1-ff9b-5d58-8736-f6d088f0fbff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} \\\\ 3x\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530041} {:answer/id #uuid "c5326a22-d486-5ce3-9922-e1b26941c409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & x & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530074} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f8b85e-be47-53f6-a0d6-ac91b60f58ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x & 3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83b07263-56a1-53d6-9f6b-dd0ec4566cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2x \\\\ 3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529908} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ff3943-ac10-594c-b82e-a6425e8c3606" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb5a1bbc-92e2-569a-8c18-7d0fed7e610f" :question/math-academy-id "q-269512" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:R\\to {R}^{3},$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ {x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{3}$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ {x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2x \\\\ 3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{3\\times 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d786586f-cacb-5781-86ff-cc8acf311dcf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Total Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12715d51-1e46-58dc-9ed7-12d504779850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529616} {:answer/id #uuid "50f86596-75fe-59b7-9ec7-2bf9eedceca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529775} {:answer/id #uuid "62d3ff2d-74e4-54a7-bd2e-09536e6dc948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529824} {:answer/id #uuid "a025fb5b-6ee3-5ae3-a624-8c215ceb9820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529977} {:answer/id #uuid "dae61b85-1333-5c21-bdf8-02a24c25d538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a025fb5b-6ee3-5ae3-a624-8c215ceb9820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529977} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eafdd0c-fbfb-51de-93e2-baad15ae52e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "752cfa47-ef2c-5a18-9f32-7e84cd447c33" :question/math-academy-id "q-269514" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:R\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{2}$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the total derivative at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15fada7f-4a9a-5e72-9699-694e302beef3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a 3-Tensor Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a76f9d5-8bc8-5cdd-9750-c5367f8d4ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a76f9d5-8bc8-5cdd-9750-c5367f8d4ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529919} :answer-field/id #uuid "65083882-b071-5cdc-b0bb-b6b399d89d5d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "085bdd72-4fe3-54d7-bc86-1b96c914a54e" :question/math-academy-id "q-269655" :question/problem "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 3}\\to {R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=A[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{31}}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{11}+{a}_{12}+4{a}_{13} \\\\ 5{a}_{21}+{a}_{22}+4{a}_{23} \\\\ 5{a}_{31}+{a}_{32}+4{a}_{33}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{31}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{31}}(5{a}_{31}+{a}_{32}+4{a}_{33})=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15fada7f-4a9a-5e72-9699-694e302beef3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a 3-Tensor Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a26531-d38a-52e9-b3c9-24c8415ea4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96a26531-d38a-52e9-b3c9-24c8415ea4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529946} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fe390c4-afd7-57df-9245-b9ef90284a05" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e0e9fc0e-4ca3-5c69-92b6-288fedf51d5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-269665" :question/problem "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to {R}^{2}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]A.\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{22}}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{11}-2{a}_{21}+3{a}_{31} & 2{a}_{12}-2{a}_{22}+3{a}_{32}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{22}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{22}}(2{a}_{12}-2{a}_{22}+3{a}_{32})=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15fada7f-4a9a-5e72-9699-694e302beef3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a 3-Tensor Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "926d713a-df65-5783-bd0c-dd44262809ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "926d713a-df65-5783-bd0c-dd44262809ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529936} :answer-field/id #uuid "7978731e-1bfd-5eec-8332-24f5f00d8343" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0562d85-9065-5ae6-9356-9eba869acb60" :question/math-academy-id "q-269667" :question/problem "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to {R}^{2}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]A.\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{a}_{32}}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{11}+{a}_{21}-2{a}_{31} & 5{a}_{12}+{a}_{22}-2{a}_{32}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{a}_{32}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{32}}(5{a}_{11}+{a}_{21}-2{a}_{31})=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15fada7f-4a9a-5e72-9699-694e302beef3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a 3-Tensor Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d6bd45e-d24b-549d-9a1c-62a7a41a0df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d6bd45e-d24b-549d-9a1c-62a7a41a0df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529860} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e16ff3f-f740-5551-904f-07d98a46fde3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2dd288c1-a4fd-5154-a46e-c65943d99445" :question/math-academy-id "q-269669" :question/problem "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 3}\\to {R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 & -5\\end{aligned}]A.\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{33}}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10{a}_{11}-6{a}_{21}-5{a}_{31}\\, & 10{a}_{12}-6{a}_{22}-5{a}_{32}\\, & 10{a}_{13}-6{a}_{23}-5{a}_{33}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{33}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{33}}(10{a}_{13}-6{a}_{23}-5{a}_{33})=-5.\n$$"}]}
